RATIONALE: A novelty_killer's GREEN gate is 'is the mechanism genuinely new?' — and the answer is no: the deterministic-default demotion is vendor-DOCUMENTED behavior (wazero WithRandSource docs) and was independently found+fixed ≥4 times per the packet's own evidence (CrowdSec PR#4495, wetware#106, wapc-go, wazero#620 — well past the ≥2-source bar). That kills mechanism novelty outright. The claim survives RED because it does not pretend the mechanism is new — it explicitly reframes the contribution as a conformance-synthesis and discloses the collisions honestly; and no single prior source owns the combined synthesis (cross-runtime anomaly across all 4 runtimes + successor-spec conformance + un-defendable-by-correct-guest). That residual synthesis is real but SoK/systematization-grade, not the new-mechanism altitude GREEN asserts. Two further drags: (a) the 'silent' framing must be narrowed — it is invisible to the GUEST but documented to the integrator, which weakens the 'no defense possible' novelty edge; (b) I could not run live ≥2-source verification (web search auth-blocked), so my collision count rests on packet citations + vendor-documented behavior from prior knowledge rather than fresh independent retrieval. Net: honest YELLOW — strong, well-evidenced, un-owned synthesis of a known, vendor-documented, repeatedly-rediscovered mechanism. Not a 6/6-GREEN novelty.
